        { "id": "b", "text": "6ab + 8a - b" },
        { "id": "c", "text": "6a^2b^2 + 2a - b" },
        { "id": "d", "text": "2ab + 2a - b" }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "a",
      "explanation": "ab terms: 4ab + 2ab = 6ab. a terms: -3a + 5a = 2a. b terms: -b. Result: 6ab + 2a - b."
    },
    {
      "id": "q3",
      "type": "multiple-choice",
      "difficulty": "application",
      "stem": "The perimeter of a triangle with sides (3x + 1), (2x - 4), and (x + 7) is:",
      "options": [
        { "id": "a", "text": "5x + 4" },
        { "id": "b", "text": "6x + 4" },
        { "id": "c", "text": "6x + 12" },
        { "id": "d", "text": "6x - 4" }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "b",
      "explanation": "Perimeter = (3x + 1) + (2x - 4) + (x + 7) = 3x + 2x + x + 1 - 4 + 7 = 6x + 4."
    },
